Well, well....This is what was called a Major bug and NOW a corrected
version of NH3.0j has been made (readily available at your nearest
ftp site in upenn.

The cause of the bug is in the memory allocation when the game was saved
and restored. In fact, to successfully retrieve the saved file, your
memory configuration must be exactly the same as when the game was saved.
ie. if the memory was 585367 bites when you saved it, it must be that
figure when you retrieve it.

With regard to copying saved files, DON'T put saved games on your 
hard drive and COMPRESS disk thereafter! The same junk will result!

